<title>UK: SkyePharma seeks U.S. heart drug approval.</title>
<headline>SkyePharma seeks U.S. heart drug approval.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>British-based drug company SkyePharma Plc said on Thursday its U.S. subsidiary Brightstone Pharma Inc had filed for American approval of a generic version of Schering-Plough Corp's heart drug Imdur.</p>
<p>In a statement Skyepharma said it had filed an  Abbreviated New Drug Application for the drug, known generically as Isosorbide Mononitrate, which lost patent protection in December 1996.  </p>
<p>Skyepharma said Brightstone had filed five separate new drug applications this year out of a pipeline of 15 drugs.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
